<title>FINLAND: Raisio falls on Monsanto plan.</title>
<headline>Raisio falls on Monsanto plan.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish food, animal feed and chemicals group Raisio fell sharply in thin early trade on Thursday on news that Monsanto Co had a licensing agreement to develop a cholesterol-lowering oil, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 1100/0900 GMT, Raisio traded at 575.00, down 32.00 markka or over five percent, but deals were quite small.</p>
<p>&quot;Raisio usually reacts strongly to news,&quot; one broker said, referring to the stock's recent normal volatility. &quot;But I believe it could come down a little more,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358 - 0 - 680 50 248</p>
